    "updated_at": "2022-03-17T17:04:31Z",
    "body": "I think panicking in this case is *definitely* the wrong action. I can think of a few alternatives that might be feasible here:\r\n\r\n- Print a message that says that `EDITOR` could not be found on `PATH`.\r\n- Ask the user to provide the path to the editor binary\r\n- Provide a flag on the command line that lets the user supply a path to the editor binary.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, it seems that all of these require that the user know about the distinction between the shell alias and binary.",
