    "body": "Thank you very much for your detailed response.\r\n\r\nI absolutely agree with you. The more i think about this issue the more i think i made a mistake referencing to the Flathub installation using `alias`. The correct approach is for surecreating a link instead, since it works shell independent.\r\n\r\nAnd as you said, there should be a *good* error message instead of a panic and i think it's worth to print the contents of `$EDITOR`/`$VISUAL` as well. A hint about the use of a \"subshell\" might not be bad as well.\r\n\r\nI don't know why but i thought `starship config` would just pass the call to the shell without spawning a subshell.",
