    "body": "The other option would be to set `VISUAL=io.neovim.nvim`, since that's what the actual binary is called, and to continue using `nvim` as a shell alias for interactive use. I'm not sure what the upsides/downsides of each are, but throwing that out there in case it proves useful.",
